<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#system-ita> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The extended Ifá reading performed for an individual at initiation (kariosha, itá de kariosha) or as a life-path consultation. Typically multi-sign, conducted by a Babalawo, and interpreted by Olorisha elders. The itá record is among the most sensitive personal documents in the tradition."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorizedPractitioner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authorized practitioner type"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#signTaboo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#DivinationSign> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#verseTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "verse theme"@en .
