<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ebo-cleansing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Spiritual cleansing"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#castingMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The physical medium used to cast or generate the sign in this system. Examples: ikin (palm nuts), okuele/ekuele (divining chain), owó dilogún (cowries), obi (coconut), obi kola (kola nut), chamalongo (coconut shells or bones). Range: iroko:CastingMediumScheme."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ebo-rogacion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cleansing and feeding of the head (ori/eleda) using specific cool and white materials. One of the most commonly prescribed works across Lucumí and related traditions."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#system-ifa> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Ifá"@es .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#DivinationVerse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A single verse, story, or pataki within a sign's corpus. In Ifá: an ese Ifá. In Dilogún: a rezo or pataki. In Fá: a hwenoho. Verses carry narrative, ethical, prescriptive, and esoteric content. They are the primary means by which divination knowledge is transmitted and applied. Verse text is initiated-elder access; the existence of a verse corpus for a sign is public."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#DivinationReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Divination Reading"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#OutcomeTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Divination Outcome Types"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-okuele> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Okuele / Ekuele"@es .
